 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 504355,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>Purple flowers (P) are dominant over white flowers (p), and long pollen grains are dominant over round pollen grains. When purple flowers and long pollen grain plants were crossed with plants with white flowers and round pollen grains, all the <span data-math=\"F_1\">F_1</span> plants showed purple flowers and long pollen grains. The <span data-math=\"F_1\">F_1</span> plants were crossed and the results are in the table. </p> \n<table style=\"margin: auto\">\n<tbody><tr>\n  <th>Phenotype</th>\n  <th>Percentage</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td>purple/long</td>\n  <td>75%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td>purple/round</td>\n  <td>5%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td>white/long</td>\n  <td>5%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td>white/round</td>\n  <td>15%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>What conclusions about the physical relationship between the traits can be drawn from the experiment?</p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 992009,
     "content_html": "The traits are probably coded by linked genes."
    },
    {
     "id": 992010,
     "content_html": "The traits follow the law of independent assortment."
    },
    {
     "id": 992011,
     "content_html": "The traits are located on different chromosomes."
    },
    {
     "id": 992012,
     "content_html": "There was epistasis."
    }
   ],
